# noor — Architecture Enforcement Rules

1. OFFLINE-ONLY: no ad SDK, no analytics SDK, no remote network call, no
   INTERNET permission in AndroidManifest.xml. No exceptions — including
   for monetization. No Play Billing / IAP library in this codebase.
2. FILE SIZE: no .dart file exceeds 150 lines.
3. LAYERING: UI widgets (presentation/) never query the database or run
   calculation logic directly. All access goes through a Cubit/Bloc in
   logic/, which calls a repository in data/.
4. ACCESSIBILITY: every interactive widget wraps in Semantics() with an
   explicit label (and value/hint where applicable).
5. RELIGIOUS TEXT: never generate Quranic text, Arabic duas, or Tamil/
   Sinhala religious strings. Source from Tanzil Project (Quran) or Hisn
   al-Muslim (Azkar) only. Flag anything unverified instead of filling
   it in.
6. DESIGN TOKENS: use lib/core/constants/app_colors.dart values only.
   Never hardcode hex colors inline. Never reintroduce the retired
   Emerald / #0A1912 palette.
7. SQL: parameterized queries only — no string-concatenated SQL.
